  ALT vs SBP          -1.6958  -11.5769  4.145e-20  Yes           -1.1577  Large effect        2.4521   1.5437

  Cohen's d here is the PAIRED effect size mean(d)/sd(d), which is the correct pairing for a CRN design.  Because CRN removes the shared seed variation, sd(d) is small and d is correspondingly large -- this is the effect WP5 quantifies.


