STEP 1  Two experiments, identical in every way but the seeding
-------------------------------------------------------------------
  arm 1 -- CRN                           replication r uses the SAME patient stream for every policy 
  arm 2 -- independent                   the policy name is mixed into the seed, so every policy sees its own streams 
  replications per policy per arm        100 
  total simulations                      1,000 

  CRN arm                    [##################################]   500/500   100.0%    9.7s elapsed,   0.0s left  
  CRN arm: 9.7 s
  independent arm            [##################################]   500/500   100.0%    7.0s elapsed,   0.0s left  
  independent arm: 7.0 s


STEP 2  CRN does not move the point estimates -- only their spread
----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Per-policy estimates under the two seeding schemes
  policy  mean (CRN)  sd (CRN)  mean (indep)  sd (indep)  difference  |diff| / SE
  ------  ----------  --------  ------------  ----------  ----------  -----------
  IFP         52.427    14.100        48.758      13.033      +3.668         2.60
  ALT         42.385    10.703        41.101       9.907      +1.284         1.20
  SBP         44.081    11.911        43.472      11.333      +0.608         0.51
  WSEPT       42.319    10.635        40.882       9.585      +1.437         1.35
  GCMU        44.049    11.303        41.937      10.887      +2.112         1.87

  largest |mean difference| between the arms 2.60 standard errors
  [OK] Every policy's mean agrees between the two arms to within 3 standard errors, and the standard deviations match.
  Theory says the two arms must agree in expectation: CRN changes the DEPENDENCE between runs, not the marginal law of any single one. It is a variance reduction technique, not a bias.


STEP 3  Correlation induced by sharing the patient stream
-------------------------------------------------------------
  pair           corr under CRN  corr under independence
  -------------  --------------  -----------------------
  IFP vs ALT            +0.9970                  +0.1033
  IFP vs SBP            +0.9960                  -0.1090
  IFP vs WSEPT          +0.9962                  -0.1060
  IFP vs GCMU           +0.9979                  +0.2544
  ALT vs SBP            +0.9973                  +0.0259
  ALT vs WSEPT          +0.9995                  -0.0085
  ALT vs GCMU           +0.9996                  -0.0328
  SBP vs WSEPT          +0.9976                  +0.1025
  SBP vs GCMU           +0.9976                  -0.0892
  WSEPT vs GCMU         +0.9994                  -0.0233

  Under independence these correlations are ~0 by construction. Under CRN they are close to +1, because a heavy week is heavy for every policy. Var(A-B) = Var(A)+Var(B)-2Cov(A,B), so the closer this gets to +1, the more of the difference's variance is cancelled.


STEP 4  Variance reduction on the pairwise differences
----------------------------------------------------------
  Pairwise differences in mean waiting time (100 replications per arm)
  comparison     mean diff (ind)  mean diff (CRN)  Var (ind)  Var (CRN)  variance removed  efficiency  CI half-w (ind)  CI half-w (CRN)  CRN reps == 100 ind
  -------------  ---------------  ---------------  ---------  ---------  ----------------  ----------  ---------------  ---------------  -------------------
